    "body": "Hi again @fujitatomoya \r\n\r\nI have debugged a bit, and I have found that the `get()` implies a `std::move`:\r\n\r\n```\r\nThread 1 \"rclcpp_1968\" hit Breakpoint 1, main (argc=1, argv=0x7ffffffee578) at /home/fmrico/ros/ros2/rolling_ws/src/ros2_test_prover/prover_rclcpp/src/rclcpp_1968.cpp:52\r\n52\t  auto a = future_result.get()->sum;\r\n(gdb) s\r\nrclcpp::detail::FutureAndRequestId<std::future<std::shared_ptr<example_interfaces::srv::AddTwoInts_Response_<std::allocator<void> > > > >::get (this=0x7ffffffed950) at /home/fmrico/ros/ros2/rolling_ws/install/rclcpp/include/rclcpp/rclcpp/client.hpp:81\r\n81\t  auto get() {return this->future.get();}\r\n(gdb) s\r\nstd::future<std::shared_ptr<example_interfaces::srv::AddTwoInts_Response_<std::allocator<void> > > >::get (this=0x7ffffffed950) at /usr/include/c++/11/future:802\r\n802\t      get()\r\n(gdb) s\r\n804\t        typename _Base_type::_Reset __reset(*this);\r\n(gdb) s\r\nstd::__basic_future<std::shared_ptr<example_interfaces::srv::AddTwoInts_Response_<std::allocator<void> > > >::_Reset::_Reset (this=0x7ffffffed820, __fut=...) at /usr/include/c++/11/future:754\r\n754\t        explicit _Reset(__basic_future& __fut) noexcept : _M_fut(__fut) { }\r\n(gdb) s\r\nstd::future<std::shared_ptr<example_interfaces::srv::AddTwoInts_Response_<std::allocator<void> > > >::get (this=0x7ffffffed950) at /usr/include/c++/11/future:805\r\n805\t        return std::move(this->_M_get_result()._M_value());\r\n```\r\nCan it invalidate the next access to the data?\r\n\r\n\r\n ",
