    "updated_at": "2022-07-14T16:15:53Z",
    "body": "`async_send_request()` returns a `future`, not a `shared_future`.\r\nTo avoid the issue, you need to get the value once and pass a copy or reference to it to all other places, or call `future.share()`.\r\nThough if you're only waiting for the future in `spin_until_future_complete()` and then getting the future, calling `future.share()` doesn't make sense (that makes sense if you're waiting for the future in more than one place, which is not the case).\r\n\r\nNote: The `get()` method of `std::future` \"extracts\" the value from it. The `get()` method of `std::shared_future` returns a reference (or const reference).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ros2/rclcpp/issues/comments/1184635014/reactions",
      "total_count": 2,
      "+1": 1,
      "-1": 0,
      "laugh": 0,
      "hooray": 0,
