    "updated_at": "2022-07-14T16:41:19Z",
    "body": "Hi @ivanpauno \r\n\r\nYes, now it is clear. \r\n\r\nI would like only to highlight that the problem arises now in (the version packaged in) Humble. In previous versions, it was perfectly possible to call `get()` many times without invaliding the pointer. I suppose many people that use services are now facing this problem migrating their software to Humble. There is no place in tutorials that warns of it. At least, this issue can be useful for many people :smile: \r\n\r\nThanks!!\r\nFrancisco",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
