    "body": "> I would like only to highlight that the problem arises now in (the version packaged in) Humble. In previous versions, it was perfectly possible to call get() many times without invaliding the pointer.\r\n\r\nYes, that was a breaking change.\r\n\r\n> There is no place in tutorials that warns of it. At least, this issue can be useful for many people smile\r\n\r\nI thought that was added to the release notes, but now that I check I don't see a comment related to it.\r\nI don't know if it makes sense to add that now, but it might be a good idea to include it there as it can help people migrate to Humble.",
